From dac08bd8ab6b7f50f7acdc46a54459b8e7a849da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OWNER NAME <owner@example.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:39:24 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] md/md-bitmap: don't create a bitmap in location_store()
 before md_run()
To: Song Liu <song@kernel.org>,
    Yu Kuai <yukuai@fygo.io>
Cc: Li Nan <magiclinan@didiglobal.com>,
    Xiao Ni <xiao@kernel.org>,
    Su Yue <glass.su@suse.com>,
    Mariusz Tkaczyk <mtkaczyk@kernel.org>,
    linux-raid@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Commit 158d32af8710 ("md-bitmap: suspend array earlier in
location_store()") dropped the mddev->pers check around the bitmap
creation in location_store(). Writing bitmap/location before the array
is started, which is how mdadm sets up the bitmap of an external
metadata array, now creates and loads a bitmap sized for an empty array,
and md_run() later creates the real one. bitmap_create() simply
overwrites mddev->bitmap, so the first struct bitmap and its pages are
leaked.

While the array is inactive only record the location, as before that
commit, and leave the creation to md_run(). An invalid setup, such as a
missing bitmap/chunksize for an external bitmap, is then reported when
the array is started, as it was before that commit.

The leak was confirmed on v7.3.3 with a debug message in bitmap_create()
reporting an already set mddev->bitmap: it fires from md_run() for every
IMSM volume with a bitmap without this patch, and not with it. This
patch was written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic; tested
together with the previous patch as described there.

Fixes: 158d32af8710 ("md-bitmap: suspend array earlier in location_store()")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # v6.7+
---
 drivers/md/md-bitmap.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/md/md-bitmap.c b/drivers/md/md-bitmap.c
index 2d82c71..922e0c9 100644
--- a/drivers/md/md-bitmap.c
+++ b/drivers/md/md-bitmap.c
@@ -2696,6 +2696,10 @@ location_store(struct mddev *mddev, const char *buf, size_t len)
 			if (!mddev_set_bitmap_ops_nosysfs(mddev))
 				goto bitmap_err;
 
+			/* md_run() creates the bitmap of an inactive array */
+			if (!mddev->pers)
+				goto done;
+
 			rv = md_bitmap_create_nosysfs(mddev);
 			if (rv)
 				goto create_err;
@@ -2712,6 +2716,7 @@ location_store(struct mddev *mddev, const char *buf, size_t len)
 				goto merge_err;
 		}
 	}
+done:
 	if (!mddev->external) {
 		/* Ensure new bitmap info is stored in
 		 * metadata promptly.
